            <ArticleTitle>Angina pectoris caused by subclavian coronary steal.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>230-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 79-year-old white woman underwent coronary bypass graft surgery using a left internal mammary artery graft. The patient represented with chest pains 4 months later. A total occlusion of the left subclavian artery was documented with a coronary subclavian steal. The patient was treated with an axillo-axillary Gore-Tex graft. Pathophysiology and therapeutic options of the coronary subclavian steal are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
